/* book exam traps: Treating λ and AFR as the same number. λ has no unit; AFR is kg of air per kg of fuel. λ = 1 means AFR = 14.7 for petrol, not 1:1. | Believing a three-way catalyst cleans any mixture. Outside its window near λ = 1, CO and HC (rich) or NOx (lean) pass through. | Forgetting light-off. A cold catalyst does almost nothing even at λ = 1; about 250 to 350 °C is needed. | Saying an oxidising catalyst removes NOx. It only burns CO and HC; NOx needs the reducing step of a three-way catalyst. | Listing CO₂ with the products of poor combustion. CO₂ comes from good combustion and is fixed by the fuel burnt; CO and HC come from poor combustion. */
